                                                                                                                                                                                 I □ species

    Global biomass is the total mass of living material,
    such as animals and plants, on Earth. A team of
     scientists estimated the global biomass, by species,
    of various wild land mammals. The team found
    that the species with the highest global biomass is
    theblank

   Which choice most effectively uses data from the
    graph to complete the sentence?

   A)  wild boar.

    B)  eastern gray kangaroo.

   C)  African bush elephant.

   D)  white-tailed deer.','Escolha a melhor alternativa para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[{"key": "A", "text": "wild boar."}, {"key": "B", "text": "eastern gray kangaroo."}, {"key": "C", "text": "African bush elephant."}, {"key": "D", "text": "white-tailed deer."}]'::jsonb,'multiple-choice',ARRAY['D']::text[],'Choice D is the best answer because it accurately identifies the species with the highest global biomass, the white-tailed deer at approximately 2.7 million metric tons. The graph shows the global biomass for four wild land mammal species with the highest global biomass. The graph indicates that the African bush elephant’s global biomass is about 1.3 million metric tons, the eastern gray kangaroo’s is about 0.6 million metric tons, and the wild boar’s is about 1.9 million metric tons. These values are all lower than the global biomass for the white-tailed deer’s approximately 2.7 million metric tons. Thus, the white-tailed deer is the species with the highest global biomass.','/sat-assets/practice-10/rw-m2-q11.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-10-digital.pdf',22,'published'),
('practice-10-paper','reading-writing',2,12,'- 12 - - - -
           Number and Origin of Clamshell Tools Found at Different
                      Levels Below the Surface in Neanderthal Cave
 Depth of tools found below Clamshells that Neanderthals Clamshells that Neanderthals
