   A right triangle has legs with lengths of

    24 centimeters and 21 centimeters. If the length of
     this triangle’s hypotenuse, in centimeters, can be
    written in the form 3 d , where d is an integer, what

     is the value of d ?','Digite sua resposta para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[]'::jsonb,'numeric',ARRAY['113']::text[],'The correct answer is 113. It’s given that the legs of a right triangle have lengths 24 centimeters and 21 centimeters. In a right triangle, the square of the length of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the lengths of the two legs. It follows that if h represents the length, in centimeters, of the hypotenuse of the right triangle, h 24 21 2 2 2 = + . This equation is equivalent to , h 1 017 2= . Taking the square root of each side of this equation yields , h 1 017 = . This equation can be rewritten as h 9 113 $ = , or h 113 9$ = . This equation is equivalent to h 3 113 = . It’s given that the length of the triangle’s hypotenuse, in centimeters, can be written in the form d 3 . It follows that the value of d is 113.','/sat-assets/practice-10/math-m1-q21.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-10-digital.pdf',41,'published'),
