          2          2
   D) x + (y −9) = 16','Escolha a melhor alternativa para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[{"key": "A", "text": "(x −8) + (y −8) = 16 2 2"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(x −8) + (y −4) = 16 2 2"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(x −4) + (y −9) = 16 2 2"}, {"key": "D", "text": "x + (y −9) = 16"}]'::jsonb,'multiple-choice',ARRAY['C']::text[],'Choice C is correct. The graph of the equation x h y k r 2 2 2 - + - = ^ ^ h h in the xy-plane is a circle with center ,h k ^ h and a radius of length r. The radius of a circle is the distance from the center of the circle to any point on the circle. If a circle in the xy-plane intersects the y-axis at exactly one point, then the perpendicular distance from the center of the circle to this point on the y-axis must be equal to the length of the circle’s radius. It follows that the x-coordinate of the circle’s center must be equivalent to the length of the circle’s radius. In other words, if the graph of x h y k r 2 2 2 - + - = ^ ^ h h is a circle that intersects the y-axis at exactly one point, then r h = must be true. The equation in choice C is x y 4 9 16 2 2 - + - = ^ ^ h h , or x y 4 9 4 2 2 2 - + - = ^ ^ h h . This equation is in the form x h y k r 2 2 2 - + - = ^ ^ h h , where h 4 = , k 9 = , and r 4 = , and represents a circle in the xy-plane with center , 4 9 ^ h and radius of length 4. Substituting 4 for r and 4 for h in the equation r h = yields 4 4 = , or 4 4 = , which is true. Therefore, the equation in choice C represents a circle in the xy-plane that intersects the y-axis at exactly one point.','/sat-assets/practice-10/math-m1-q23.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-10-digital.pdf',41,'published'),
('practice-10-paper','math',1,24,'-24 -------
    In triangles ABC and DEF, angles B and E each
    have measure 27° and angles C and F each have
    measure 41°. Which additional piece of information
     is sufficient to determine whether triangle ABC is
    congruent to triangle DEF ?

   A) The measure of angle A

    B) The length of side AB

   C) The lengths of sides BC and EF

   D) No additional information is necessary.','Escolha a melhor alternativa para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[{"key": "A", "text": "The measure of angle A"}, {"key": "B", "text": "The length of side AB"}, {"key": "C", "text": "The lengths of sides BC and EF"}, {"key": "D", "text": "No additional information is necessary."}]'::jsonb,'multiple-choice',ARRAY['C']::text[],'Choice C is correct. Since angles B and E each have the same measure and angles C and F each have the same measure, triangles ABC and DEF are similar, where side BC corresponds to side EF. To determine whether two similar triangles are congruent, it is sufficient to determine whether one pair of corresponding sides are congruent. Therefore, to determine whether triangles ABC and DEF are congruent, it is sufficient to determine whether sides BC and EF have equal length. Thus, the lengths of BC and EF are sufficient to determine whether triangle ABC is congruent to triangle DEF.','/sat-assets/practice-10/math-m1-q24.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-10-digital.pdf',41,'published'),
