   What is the perimeter, in inches, of a rectangle with a
    length of 4 inches and a width of 9 inches?

   A) 13

    B)  17

   C) 22

   D) 26','Escolha a melhor alternativa para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[{"key": "A", "text": "13"}, {"key": "B", "text": "17"}, {"key": "C", "text": "22"}, {"key": "D", "text": "26"}]'::jsonb,'multiple-choice',ARRAY['D']::text[],'Choice D is correct. The perimeter of a figure is equal to the sum of the measurements of the sides of the figure. It’s given that the rectangle has a length of 4 inches and a width of 9 inches. Since a rectangle has 4 sides, of which opposite sides are parallel and equal, it follows that the rectangle has two sides with a length of 4 inches and two sides with a width of 9 inches. Therefore, the perimeter of this rectangle is 4 4 9 9 + + + , or 26 inches.','/sat-assets/practice-10/math-m2-q04.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-10-digital.pdf',47,'published'),
